  "background": "scribe",
  "backstory": "Deep within the subterranean archives of the gnomish redoubt of Mithral Deep, there once worked a master scribe who knew every secret of the ancient libraries—yet whose own name is now entirely absent from their pages. Gifted with the sharp sight of the deep-dwellers and a keen mind naturally shielded against arcane deceits, they spent decades classifying the forgotten relics of history. They possessed an uncanny knack for tinkering, translating the dry formulas of long-dead artificers into delicate clockwork music boxes that whistled the forgotten anthems of fallen empires. But when they unearthed a heavily redacted chronicle detailing a silent, encroaching shadow destined to swallow the surface world, they made a perilous choice. To protect their kin from the eyes of those who wished this truth buried, the scribe penned a final, self-erasing rune over their own name in the great census scrolls, vanishing into the darkness of the tunnels as a ghost with a blank ledger.\n\nNo longer a mere keeper of books, the nameless gnome realized that ink could be spilled and parchment burned, but a song, once set free, lives forever in the minds of the living. They forged a wondrous lute of brass and elderwood, fitted with intricate, self-winding gears of their own invention that could hum with the resonant, magical frequencies of the cosmos. They became a bard not of cheap tavern-tales, but a chronicler of fate, weaving ancient lore into powerful spells of protection and inspiration. Driven by the absolute necessity to find the missing pieces of this apocalyptic history, they now wander the surface kingdoms. They seek to rally heroes and document their deeds, knowing that in the grand design of the world, even the smallest gear—and the most forgotten scribe—can turn the tides of destiny.",
